From: VUX9K
Subject: [PATCH] iomap: ioend mempools of 2 entries

The block layer selects FS_IOMAP, whose ioend biosets each reserve
4 * (PAGE_SIZE / SECTOR_SIZE) bios with BIO_MAX_VECS vecs at boot: ~256 KB
of unmovable slab in a kernel that has 8 MB and keeps contiguous blocks free
for every exec (noMMU, FLAT). No filesystem here writes back through iomap
(vfat uses buffer heads), so 2 entries each keep the forward-progress
guarantee for the rare user. This tree's own patch, not sent upstream
(docs/agents/linux.md, "Kernel patches").

---
diff --git a/fs/iomap/ioend.c b/fs/iomap/ioend.c
index 7bbbb41..77570b8 100644
--- a/fs/iomap/ioend.c
+++ b/fs/iomap/ioend.c
@@ -514,7 +514,12 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(iomap_split_ioend);
 
 static int __init iomap_ioend_init(void)
 {
-	const unsigned int nr_mempool_entries = 4 * (PAGE_SIZE / SECTOR_SIZE);
+	/*
+	 * VUX9K: 2, not 4 * (PAGE_SIZE / SECTOR_SIZE): each entry keeps a bio with
+	 * BIO_MAX_VECS vecs from boot on, ~256 KB for the two sets, and no filesystem
+	 * here writes back through iomap (vfat uses buffer heads)
+	 */
+	const unsigned int nr_mempool_entries = 2;
 	int error;
 
 	error = bioset_init(&iomap_ioend_bioset, nr_mempool_entries,
